# Fill in the author(s) and, once a release is archived, the DOI and version.
# GitHub shows "Cite this repository" from this file.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "GridSense Simulator: hosting capacity of distributed PV by deterministic, stochastic and quasi-static time-series methods"
abstract: >-
  Experimental infrastructure for comparing hosting-capacity methods on
  low-voltage networks under regulatory voltage criteria (ANEEL PRODIST
  Module 8 and EN 50160), with open datasets, frozen experiment protocols and
  per-result provenance.
authors:
  - name: "GridSense Contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/EngEleLuiz/Gridsense-simulator"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - hosting capacity
  - photovoltaic generation
  - low-voltage distribution networks
  - quasi-static time series
  - power quality
  - PRODIST
  - EN 50160
